        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kurt Julian Weill, Bertolt Brecht, John Gay, Elisabeth Hauptmann\n- Works: The Threepenny Opera, The Beggar's Opera\n- Places: Germany, United States\n- Topics: Composition, theater adaptation, play with music\n\nFacts:\n- Kurt Julian Weill was a German composer active in Germany from the 1920s and later in the United States.\n- Kurt Julian Weill and Bertolt Brecht developed theatrical productions together.\n- The Threepenny Opera is the best-known work associated with Kurt Julian Weill in this chunk.\n- The Threepenny Opera is a play with music by Bertolt Brecht.\n- The Threepenny Opera was adapted from John Gay's 18th-century English ballad opera The Beggar's Opera.\n- Elisabeth Hauptmann was involved in the adaptation of The Beggar's Opera into The Threepenny Opera.",
