        "original_id": "27aade14-cd6c-5a48-9f98-d685dca05e1e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kurt Weill, Bertolt Brecht, Elisabeth Hauptmann, John Gay, François Villon, Rudyard Kipling\n- Works: The Threepenny Opera, The Beggar's Opera, Mack the Knife\n- Concepts: play with music, ballad opera, adaptation\n\nFacts:\n- John Gay wrote the 18th-century English ballad opera The Beggar's Opera.\n- Kurt Weill developed productions with Bertolt Brecht, including his best-known work The Threepenny Opera.\n- The Threepenny Opera is a play with music by Bertolt Brecht and Elisabeth Hauptmann.\n- The Threepenny Opera was adapted from John Gay's The Beggar's Opera.\n- The Threepenny Opera includes music by Kurt Weill.\n- The Threepenny Opera includes insertion ballads by François Villon and Rudyard Kipling.\n- The Threepenny Opera included the ballad Mack the Knife.",
